    "title": "Emma Stone’s Backless Oscars Gown Took 600 Hours of Beadwork",
    "text": "2 min readEmma Stone is as lovely as ever in Louis Vuitton at the 2026 Oscars.The actor looked oh-so romantic in a silver dress with a scooped neckline, micro sleeves, and an open back. The beading on the dress was so intricate, it took 600 hours of work. Little diamond earrings and shimmery silver shadow perfectly finished off the look.Mike Coppola//Getty ImagesIt was a contrast, in terms of color, to her last red-carpet look, a bubblegum-pink slipdress and cardigan from the French fashion house (of which she is an ambassador), which she wore to the Actor Awards earlier this month.Mike Coppola//Getty ImagesAdvertisement - Continue Reading BelowStone has showered us with fashion as she’s made her way through this year’s awards season. It’s been a big one for Stone, who has been widely recognized for her performance in the sci-fi thriller Bugonia. The star has referred to her role in the movie as one of the most “physically challenging” she’s had, yet she’s described the entire filming experience as “amazing.”Mike Coppola//Getty ImagesAt the BAFTAs, she was nominated for Best Leading Actress. At the Golden Globes, she received a nod for Best Performance by a Female Actor in a Motion Picture—Musical or Comedy. At the Actor Awards (formerly the SAG Awards), she was nominated for Female Actor in a Leading Role.And at tonight’s ceremony, she is up for two Oscars, for Best Actress and Best Picture (as a producer), making her the youngest woman to earn seven career Oscar nominations.Stone has won two Best Actress Oscars in her career—for La La Land (2017) and Yorgos Lanthimos’s Poor Things (2024). Bugonia is her latest collaboration with the Greek filmmaker.",
